  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0007_4ecce7915d0a.png\"/><br >To draw the inequality, let us draw the equation<br ><math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br >For point of intersection<br >(i) <math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>8,1</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br >(ii) <math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi> </mi><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi> </mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi> </mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br >(iii) <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>D</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi> </mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br >Now <math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⇒</mo></math> region which contains origin<br ><math><mi>y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo></math> region above line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br ><math><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⇒</mo></math> region outside the parabola<br >Now required area<br >Method I:<br >Using x-axis:<br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></munderover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∫</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></munderover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math><br ><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br ><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></math><br >Method II:<br >Using y-axis:<br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></munderover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>y</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></math><br ><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></math><br >Note: The question should include bounded area term as in <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math> quadrant there exist a area which satisfy the inequality and is unbounded."
